      "Language": "nor",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In Norway the first percutaneously, transluminally placed human coronary artery endoprosthesis (stent) was implanted in the spring of 1991. This article summarizes international experience of treatment with the Palmaz-Schatz balloon expandable stent for coronary use and describes the first two patients treated with such implants at Ullevål hospital."},
